` into `fields` wholesale with no no-op filtering (batch_dispatch.py:155-161, 189-195), so a field only fails to 'survive' when `changed` is already empty — a case the existing `if changed:` guard at differ.py:598 already suppresses. As written the change would be a no-op and leave the ~516 mutations in place.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2f334af2ea2c73ba","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'skip the branch-3 `_emit` only when the resolved `changed` dict contains no field that survives `_mutation_to_batch_dict`'","norm_id":"n8ed458e1a507c67f","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Key-set prev where branch-3 populates `changed` with resolved values that equal the Jira side — the predicate keeps emitting them"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Define inert as: for every field in `changed`, `changed[field] == jira_fields.get(field)` (after EXCLUDED/label filtering). Skip the branch-3 `_emit` when that holds for all fields; keep emitting whenever any resolved field differs from its Jira value.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the Why ('empty local_fields') and Approach ('resolved==Jira') characterisations of the inert set, and state explicitly how a state field resolving to None (local_fields empty) is classified — inert-and-skipped, or a real payload — since resolve_state returns None which differs from the Jira value.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["conflict_resolver.py:47-49 resolve_state returns local_val (None when local_fields empty)","differ.py:591-597: field enters `changed` whenever local_val != jira_val; state fields take `local_val` (None), which != jira_val","resolving None-for-state is neither 'equal to Jira' nor a benign no-op — it is a destructive blank-out"],"finding":"The plan blames the ~516 mutations on 'an empty `local_fields`' (Why section), but the Approach's no-op criterion may not cover that case. With empty `local_fields`, state-class fields (status/assignee/priority/title/type) resolve via `resolve_state` to `local_val = None`, which differs from the Jira value — so `changed` is non-empty and the resolved value is NOT equal to the Jira side. Under the concrete-example criterion ('resolver returns exactly the Jira-side value') these fields would NOT be classified inert, so the emit would not be skipped for the very case named as the source.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8ba6c791cc27b42a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Why section ('empty `local_fields`') vs Approach concrete example ('conflict resolver returns exactly the Jira-side value for every changed field')","norm_id":"n19f7b035256931ab","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Key-set prev, key present in both, Jira entry has a non-empty status/priority/title; local_fields empty → changed={status:None,...}, not equal to Jira, not skipped"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Clarify whether branch-3 will literally call `batch_dispatch._mutation_to_batch_dict` (adding a new dependency to the pure differ, and enumerating that module in Files) or replicate its field-survival logic inline within differ.py, and reconcile with differ.py's 'no I/O/globals' purity contract.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.566,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Files: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/differ.py`, tests","batch_dispatch.py:119 `def _mutation_to_batch_dict(mutation) -> dict:` — the sole definition; applier.py:139 and apply_outbound.py:33 merely import it","differ.py:27 docstring: 'The function is pure: no I/O, no time/random, no logging, no globals.'","differ.py has no batch_dispatch import (grep: no matches)"],"finding":"The approach hinges on `_mutation_to_batch_dict`, but that symbol is defined in batch_dispatch.py (re-exported into applier.py/apply_outbound.py), not in differ.py — the only source file in scope. differ.py is documented as a pure function with no I/O/globals and does not currently import batch_dispatch, so literally invoking _mutation_to_batch_dict would introduce an unenumerated cross-module dependency (batch_dispatch -> mutation_payloads); alternatively the plan intends to replicate the field-survival test inline. The plan does not say which.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff964df69e21de72b","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section / Files section","norm_id":"n6d186f7cfc4e650c","priority":0.134,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer wires differ.py to call batch_dispatch._mutation_to_batch_dict, adding a new module load in the pure differ","Implementer instead inlines the survival check but the plan's wording implies a direct call, causing divergence between plan and edit"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the survival test is computed inline in differ.py over the resolved `changed` dict (mirroring _mutation_to_batch_dict's field selection) so no batch_dispatch import is added; or, if a direct call is intended, add batch_dispatch.py to the Files list and confirm loading it keeps compute_mutations pure.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable